cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Lacuna: reproducible brain lesion network mapping"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Petersen
    given-names: Marvin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6426-7167"
    affiliation: "University Medical Center Utrecht"
  - family-names: Biessels
    given-names: Geert Jan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6862-2496"
    affiliation: "University Medical Center Utrecht"
repository-code: "https://github.com/m-petersen/lacuna"
url: "https://lacuna-py.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  Lacuna is a scientific Python package and BIDS-App for reproducible brain
  lesion network mapping. It implements functional and structural network
  mapping, accelerated functional network mapping, focal damage, and parcel
  aggregation analyses on standardized MNI reference spaces, fetching the
  required normative connectomes, templates, and atlases on demand.
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-06-10"
keywords:
  - neuroimaging
  - lesion analysis
  - lesion network mapping
  - brain mapping
  - BIDS
